format: calibrator-session
version: 1
session:
  session_id: cal-2026-10-03-s8
  generated_at: "2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  generator: "firstmate crewmate calibrator-policy-g8 (Claude Opus 5.5), Calibrator generation policy (yujieteo/calibrator docs/generation-policy.md at c7e2534, PR 3), selected by impact and feasibility with the health baseline first; no category quotas; 16 cards, short of the default 100 by choice of strong candidates"
  inputs: "my health baseline as stated 3 October 2026 (15,000 steps daily, daily swimming); data/notes.md and data/calibrator/raw.toon at yujieteo/site@6a17046 (sessions to cal-2026-10-02-s6, 605 answered); published unanswered session cal-2026-10-02-s7 at yujieteo/calibrator@e6e7ff5; site commit history 1 to 3 October and data/about/about.yaml at 6a17046; public research, health and weather sources and Claude Code and Apple documentation, retrieved 2026-10-03T02:50:00Z"
questions[16]{question_id,session_id,proposition,context,high_action,low_action,origin,info_gain,action_impact,novelty,adversariality,relevance,explore_exploit,resolution_rule,resolution_horizon,resolution_status,outcome,resolution_evidence,generated_at}:
  cal-20261003-s8-001,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"Will my phone's step history show at least 15,000 steps on every day from Saturday 3 to Friday 9 October?","15,000 steps a day is my baseline. No note records my daily steps, so whether it already holds is unknown, not missed.",keep the routine and read the week's step history on 10 October,read the last seven days' steps tonight and name the kind of day that falls short,notes,90,88,40,50,98,exploit,"True if step records for 3 to 9 October show 15,000 or more on all seven days; false if any day shows fewer; unresolved if a day has no record. Resolves execution only, not any metabolic benefit.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-002,cal-2026-10-03-s8,Will I swim on each of the seven days from Saturday 3 to Friday 9 October?,"Daily swimming is my baseline. No note records my swims, so a gap in the notes says nothing about a missed day.",keep the swim slot and log each swim in one line,name tonight the day most likely to break it and book a second slot that day,notes,88,86,40,50,98,exploit,"True if a swim log, workout record or my own report covers all seven days; false if I report a day without a swim; unresolved otherwise. Resolves execution only, not any metabolic benefit.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-003,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"From 5 to 11 October, with no crewmate launched or reviewed in one fixed two-hour window kept for walking and swimming, will I meet both parts of my baseline on at least six of the seven days?","Hypothesis: fleet work competes with the baseline. 50, 80 and, by 10:30 on 3 October, 50 site commits landed on 1 to 3 October, and I gave 97% that agent work made me skip a strength session (s4-031). Tests feasibility, not health effect.",name the window tonight and have firstmate hold decisions in it from 5 to 11 October,keep my hours as they are and note what displaced each missed day,synthesis,88,90,60,82,95,exploit,"True if the window was kept and step and swim records show both parts met on at least six of 5 to 11 October; false if it was kept and fewer days met both; unresolved if the window was not kept or records are missing. Shows success under the window, not that the window caused it.",2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-004,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"On at least three of the five weekdays from 5 to 9 October, will walking 15,000 steps and swimming, with travel, take more than three hours?","At about 100 steps a minute, a brisk pace, 15,000 steps is around 150 minutes of walking, less what daily life already gives. If the baseline costs three hours, something else gives way; better to name it than let it be chosen by default.","name tonight which daily activity gives up the time, and tell firstmate",plan the week as now,synthesis,84,84,70,78,92,explore,"True if my log or report of 5 to 9 October shows more than three hours on walking, swimming and travel on at least three weekdays; false if it shows three hours or less on at least three; unresolved otherwise.",2026-10-10,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-005,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"By 31 October, will I have asked a doctor whether a blood test such as HbA1c and a lipid panel should be done now, as a baseline for my activity routine?","Without a measurement, no card can tell whether walking and swimming change my metabolic health. HbA1c reflects about three months of blood glucose. Healthier SG Screening may cover some tests; my eligibility is unknown.",book a family-doctor visit by 16 October and ask,raise it at my next routine doctor's visit,synthesis,86,80,72,60,94,explore,True if a note or my own report says I asked a doctor by 31 October; false if I report I did not; unresolved otherwise. The results stay private and are not needed to resolve this.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-006,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"In the week of 5 October, will I walk for at least ten minutes within half an hour after dinner on at least five days?","Light walking breaks lowered post-meal glucose compared with sitting in short lab studies. Those are acute markers, not long-term change. Walking after dinner also puts steps where they cost least.",walk after dinner from 5 October and count the days,keep the weekday after-lunch walk and find the steps elsewhere,news,78,80,55,45,90,exploit,True if my report shows at least five such walks from 5 to 11 October; false if fewer; unresolved otherwise. Any metabolic benefit stays unverified.,2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-007,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"Between 5 and 18 October, will lightning or a thunderstorm stop at least one outdoor swim I had planned?","October and November bring Singapore's afternoon and early-evening thunderstorms and the most lightning days, and SportSG closes ActiveSG pools on NEA lightning data. Whether my pool is outdoors is not in my notes.","move planned swims before 11:00 where I can, and check myENV before leaving",keep my swim times as they are,news,80,78,78,50,90,explore,True if a note or my report records a planned outdoor swim stopped by weather from 5 to 18 October; false if I report every planned swim went ahead or stopped for other reasons; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-19,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-008,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"In the week of 5 October, will I handle at least one firstmate review or decision a day from my phone while walking, through Claude Code's Remote Control?","Remote Control lets the Claude phone app continue a Claude Code session running on my Mac; it is a research preview, and I may already use it. It could turn desk supervision into walking time, or pull my attention from the walk.",start firstmate's session with Remote Control on 5 October and try one walking review,keep reviews at the desk and walk without them,news,78,76,80,55,88,explore,True if my report shows a walking review on at least five of 5 to 11 October; false if fewer; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-009,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"If I start no new visualisation or port from 5 to 18 October, will I name by 19 October something specific that the pause cost me?","About 180 site commits landed from 1 to 3 October, mostly ports and visualisations. Hypothesis: the gallery is the fleet's main pull on my hours. A pause frees supervision time; the cost is momentum on work I enjoy.",keep porting within October's cap of eight,pause new visualisations and ports from 5 to 18 October and give the time to the baseline,synthesis,82,86,65,92,86,explore,"Unresolved if no pause happens. If it does: true if a note by 19 October names a specific cost; false if my report says it cost nothing specific.",2026-10-19,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-010,cal-2026-10-03-s8,Will a phone Shortcut that saves today's step count to a file each evening run on at least five of the seven days from 12 to 18 October?,"Shortcuts' Find Health Samples action can read step counts, and others have exported them this way. If it works, a firstmate hook could hold new launches on a short-step day. Untested here; low odds, cheap to try.","build the Shortcut by 11 October, then brief a crewmate for a launch-hold hook",skip it and read steps in the Health app by eye,news,76,70,88,60,84,explore,True if the saved file holds a step count for at least five of 12 to 18 October; false if fewer; unresolved if the trial never starts.,2026-10-19,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-011,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"In the week of 5 October, will both ten-minute home strength sessions happen without costing a day of the swim or the steps?",WHO's 2020 guidelines add muscle strengthening on two or more days a week to aerobic activity. I gave 91% to two ten-minute home sessions from 5 October (s6-030); their days are not yet named.,put both sessions on named days before 5 October,do one session a week in October and keep the baseline whole,calibration,74,74,40,45,86,exploit,True if my report shows two strength sessions from 5 to 11 October with the baseline met on those days; false if fewer than two; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-12,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-012,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"If I answer at most one Calibrator session a week from 5 October, will at least half of the actions I choose from them be done by their dates by 31 October?",Seven 100-card sessions came out on 2 October and session 7 is still unanswered. I gave 90% that I answer to feel decisive more than to change what I do (s6-089). Fewer sessions trade breadth for doing.,cap sessions at one a week from 5 October,"keep a session as soon as the last is recorded, with fewer cards each",calibration,80,80,60,88,86,explore,True if a note by 1 November counts the actions I chose from capped sessions and at least half were done by their dates; false if fewer; unresolved if the cap was not kept or no count exists.,2026-11-01,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-013,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"By 16 October, will I have chosen, in my own words, at least two actions from this session's cards?","From this session an answer is a belief, not an endorsement; an action counts only when I choose it. This is the first test of whether a shorter, health-first session yields choices.",keep sessions short and ranked by impact,ask myself before session 9 why no card was worth choosing,calibration,76,70,50,60,84,explore,True if notes by 16 October record at least two actions from cal-2026-10-03-s8 that I chose myself; false if fewer; unresolved if session 8 is never answered.,2026-10-16,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-014,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"If I invite one friend to walk or swim with me in the week of 5 October, will we go together a second time by 18 October?",It joins two things I value. I gave 82% that a monthly meal with a friend does more for my long-term health than a second strength morning (s6-013). Whether company keeps me going is untested.,invite one friend by 6 October,keep walking and swimming alone,synthesis,68,66,60,40,80,explore,Unresolved if no invitation is made. Otherwise true if a note or my report records a second joint walk or swim by 18 October; false if not.,2026-10-19,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-015,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"On at least two weekdays from 5 to 16 October, will NEA's heat stress level read high when I set out on the after-lunch walk?","The weekday walk falls near the day's peak heat. myENV shows a low, moderate or high heat stress level from wet-bulb globe temperature; a covered route would keep the steps on high days.",pick a covered or air-conditioned route for high days by 5 October,keep the outdoor route and check only when it feels hot,news,62,62,70,40,80,explore,"True if checks of myENV on walk days, noted or reported, show high on at least two; false if they show high on fewer, with at least five days checked; unresolved otherwise.",2026-10-17,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
  cal-20261003-s8-016,cal-2026-10-03-s8,"By 31 October, will I need step or swim data beyond the phone's own weekly summary to decide a change to my routine?","A private chart of my steps and swims would be fun to build, but costs a crewmate and upkeep, and the phone's own records may already be enough. Build one only if a real decision needs it.",brief a crewmate for a private step-and-swim chart in November,use the phone's weekly summary and build nothing,synthesis,60,58,50,55,78,exploit,True if a note by 31 October names a routine decision that needed more than the weekly summary; false if my report says the summary sufficed; unresolved otherwise.,2026-10-31,unresolved,null,null,"2026-10-03T03:00:00Z"
