claims[32]{question_id,source_id,claim}:
  cal-20261003-s8-001,baseline,"My baseline is 15,000 steps every day and a swim every day."
  cal-20261003-s8-001,notes,No note up to this commit records a daily step count.
  cal-20261003-s8-002,baseline,My baseline includes a swim every day.
  cal-20261003-s8-002,notes,No note up to this commit records a swim.
  cal-20261003-s8-003,commits,"50 commits landed on main on 1 October, 80 on 2 October and 50 on 3 October by 10:33 SGT."
  cal-20261003-s8-003,raw,I gave 97% that I skipped a strength session in the week to 2 October because of agent work (cal-20261002-s4-031).
  cal-20261003-s8-003,baseline,"My baseline is 15,000 steps and a swim every day."
  cal-20261003-s8-004,cadence,"In 21 to 40 year olds, about 100 steps a minute marks moderate-intensity walking."
  cal-20261003-s8-004,baseline,"My baseline is 15,000 steps and a swim every day."
  cal-20261003-s8-005,a1c,The A1C test shows the average blood glucose level over the previous three months.
  cal-20261003-s8-005,hsg,"Healthier SG Screening includes cardiovascular risk screening; eligibility depends on age, sex, pre-existing conditions and the last screening date."
  cal-20261003-s8-006,buffey,"Interrupting prolonged sitting with light-intensity walking reduced post-meal glucose compared with uninterrupted sitting in adults, in acute studies."
  cal-20261003-s8-006,raw,I gave 92% that a 30-minute walk after lunch on weekdays from 5 October would be easier to keep than either strength morning (cal-20261002-s6-050).
  cal-20261003-s8-007,mss,"Thunderstorms, at times severe, occur in the afternoon and early evening in the October to November inter-monsoon period."
  cal-20261003-s8-007,mss,"October and November have about 21 to 22 mean lightning days, among the most of the year."
  cal-20261003-s8-007,mccy,SportSG uses real-time information from NEA's Lightning Information Service to decide the closure of ActiveSG swimming pools.
  cal-20261003-s8-007,about,I am based in Singapore.
  cal-20261003-s8-008,rc,Remote Control connects claude.ai/code or the Claude app for iOS and Android to a Claude Code session running on your machine.
  cal-20261003-s8-009,commits,"180 commits landed on main from 1 October to 10:33 SGT on 3 October; 141 of their subjects name a visualisation, port, pin or restyle."
  cal-20261003-s8-009,raw,I gave 100% that I enjoyed most of the week's work to 2 October (cal-20261002-s4-044).
  cal-20261003-s8-010,shortcuts,Find actions in Shortcuts include Find Health Samples.
  cal-20261003-s8-010,heckel,A Shortcut can read Health samples such as step counts and send them outside the Health app.
  cal-20261003-s8-011,who,Adults should also do muscle-strengthening activities at moderate or greater intensity on two or more days a week.
  cal-20261003-s8-011,raw,I gave 91% that two ten-minute strength sessions at home each week from 5 October would happen more often than two gym mornings (cal-20261002-s6-030).
  cal-20261003-s8-012,sessions,Seven generated sessions of 100 cards each are dated 2 October 2026.
  cal-20261003-s8-012,raw,I gave 90% that I answer Calibrator to feel decisive more than to change what I do (cal-20261002-s6-089).
  cal-20261003-s8-013,policy,"A probability answer is a belief, not an action selection; an action becomes a decision only when the person separately chooses it."
  cal-20261003-s8-014,raw,I gave 82% that a standing monthly meal with one friend would do more for my long-term health than the second strength morning (cal-20261002-s6-013).
  cal-20261003-s8-015,heat,"NEA's Heat Stress Advisory has three levels, low, moderate and high, based on wet-bulb globe temperature, and is on the myENV app and weather.gov.sg."
  cal-20261003-s8-015,about,I am based in Singapore.
  cal-20261003-s8-016,baseline,"My baseline is 15,000 steps and a swim every day."
  cal-20261003-s8-016,notes,No note up to this commit records step or swim data.